           <p class="film-notice"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10.29 3.86 1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0Z"/><path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01"/></svg>Contains horror imagery that some viewers may find disturbing.</p>
           <div class="project-desc prose">
 <p>A 56 second horror short about grief. A woman carries her late father&#39;s ashes up his old trail,
 and on his ranger radio a voice that sounds like him starts giving her directions.</p>
 <p>Made with AI, most of its shots with Veo 3.1. The story and the camera follow research I did into
 <a href="/research/horror-cinematography-shot-by-shot" data-visits-event="doc-horror-cinematography-shot-by-shot">how horror directors build dread shot by shot</a>.</p>
